{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":45320987,"ns":0,"title":"Furstenberg boundary","extract":"In mathematics, specifically harmonic analysis and probability theory, the Furstenberg boundary is a notion of boundary associated with a group.  It is named for Harry Furstenberg, who introduced it in a series of papers beginning in 1963 (in the case of semisimple Lie groups).","description":"Notion of boundary associated with a group","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}